  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions`. Its description starts \"Use when Habeas evidence needs creating or refreshing, or when `habeas coverage` or `habeas status` reports Habeas findings…\". It also quotes the user's likely words, \"the habeas test is failing\". That states when to use the skill in terms of the user's task, which meets the MUST. The description also says to use habeas-refactor first when evidence went stale because code or requirements moved. The requirement permits naming another bundled skill to avoid confusion, so this is allowed. No violation matches were listed, and I found no gap.",
